      "answer": "Two-phase drop-in: first phase, quick triage on sidewalk where neighbors vote \"Fix\" or \"Parts\" with colored dots, reducing decision paralysis. Second phase, only \"Fix\" objects move indoors. Pairs rotate every 15 minutes. Safeguard: any object untouched after two rotations automatically becomes parts. Success: count parts harvested vs objects discarded; target 1 kg of reusable hardware saved."
    },
    {
      "id": "C",
      "kind": "exploratory",
      "mechanism": "Skill-share ladder: skilled volunteers wear colored armbands and only intervene when asked. Novices start with simple tasks; armband holder coaches, then leaves. Unrepairable objects are photographed and logged as \"material resource\". Safeguard: no one works alone on electrical items. Success: photograph log shows ≥10 distinct parts reused in future neighborhood projects within one month.",
